Shiori for Classic Macintosh
Version @VERSION@

Search your pages in Hister and your notes in Kura from a Mac Plus or later, on System 6.0.8 or System 7.

What you need
- MacTCP 2.0.6 or later, on Ethernet.
- Hister served over plain HTTP on your network (MacTCP has no TLS), or the bridge (mac-bridge) next to an HTTPS-only Hister. Plain HTTP sends your searches and Hister's token unencrypted: use it only on a network you trust (docs/classic.md).

Installing
- Shiori: copy it anywhere.
- Shiori Search, the desk accessory: on System 6, install it with Font/DA Mover. On System 7, open it and drag Shiori Search to the System Folder.

First run
Preferences opens: choose Directly (HTTP) or Through mac-bridge, then enter Hister's address (http://<IP address>:<port>/), Kura's if you have one, and the token: Hister's own directly, the room token through the bridge. They stay on this Mac, in Shiori Preferences. Keep that file off shared disks: the tokens are in it.

